Problem: Spent significant time trying to override Quarto’s inline styles with CSS !important rules.
Solution: Remove problematic Quarto configurations (like image-height) that generate inline styles, then let CSS work naturally.





# ❌ WRONG - Forces inline styles
listing:
  image-height: 150px  # Generates style="height: 150px;"

# ✅ CORRECT - Let CSS handle sizing
listing:
  type: default
  fields: [image, title, description]
  # No image-height specified



/* ✅ Simple, works with Quarto's structure */
.thumbnail {
  width: 250px;
  height: 150px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}

.thumbnail img {
  max-width: 100%;
  max-height: 100%;
  object-fit: contain;
}

/* ❌ WRONG - Fighting Quarto */
.thumbnail img {
  height: 150px !important !important !important; /* Never works */
}







